ns":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T17:49:30-08:00","id":1353664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1352170-aeon-interview-with-line-developer-ian-watson?p=1353613#post1353613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! It\u2019s hard to find in the Apple Podcasts app because of the season breakdown. This shows up in \u201cseason 1\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for letting me know. I stopped using the Apple Podcasts app some time ago because I found it difficult to use to find the episodes I wanted to listen to. I had been using seasons to tag the type of content, not realizing that would bury newer episodes. I'll have to go through the backlog of episodes to fix it, which I should have some time to do later this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link